{"type":"npc","name":"Pruned Future","folder":"lBiU967QOX7QFRzY","system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":270,"temp":0,"max":270,"details":""},"ac":{"value":40,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["astral","chronan","common"],"details":"Telepathy 120 feet, Truespeech"},"level":{"value":16},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>When the lives of heroes, villains, tricksters, or other figures with great destinies are cut short under extraordinary circumstances, the unrealized potential can manifest as an echo of that lost future on the Astral Plane known as a pruned future. Whether cast into this state by a norn's shears, divine intervention, or the meddling of powerful aberrations, these beings are tormented by the dissonance between their failed reality and the grand potential they held in life. The last regrets of countless souls are drawn to their lamentations, empowering the pruned fate and inspiring them not to abandon the dreams of their old lives and the glory that could have been.</p><p>A pruned future that reaches the mortal realms and attempts to enact their destiny often draws the attention of entities that protect the integrity of time.</p><hr /><p>Temporal paradoxes are a rare category of spirits that arise when strong-willed individuals are separated from their rightful place in the timeline. Though they retain strong memories and emotional connections to their pasts, it is seldom possible for them to go back to where they came from. Even if they were to manage the daunting task of locating their original reality and timeline, it would fundamentally reject their return. This rejection stems from a combination of their former realities editing them out in the interest of self-stabilization and the influence of their new realities causing their old homes to recognize them as incompatible invaders. Unfortunately for temporal paradoxes, their new realities don't fully accept them either, making them vulnerable to unwelcome twists of fate.</p><p></p><h2>Temporal Dissonance</h2><p>Just as a pruned future can sort through multiple futures and choose their favorite, they are simultaneously aware and unaware of their pruned state. They both believe in the grand accomplishment of their heroic destiny and are aware that the same destiny lies in ruins, their great deeds undone. From moment to moment, the pruned future chooses either to exemplify the swaggering demigod or the tragic spirit, often as the mood strikes them.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 1,250/2,800/5,150 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (slashing), armor (light, medium), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Deception, Intimidation, Occultism)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, charisma, constitution, energy resistant (vitality), intelligence, mind, mind shield, sensory (darkvision), spells (Occult: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.SwUiVavHKMWG7t5K]{Truespeech}), spiked, spirit, strength, throwing, time, wild, winged</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Ryan King","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":9},"dex":{"mod":5},"con":{"mod":6},"int":{"mod":6},"wis":{"mod":5},"cha":{"mod":6}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":28,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"thoughtsense","acuity":"imprecise","range":120}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":30,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":28,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":28,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":27},"athletics":{"base":31},"deception":{"base":28},"intimidation":{"base":28},"occultism":{"base":32}},"traits":{"value":["astral"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"med"}}},"_id":"1t0